      },
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_root_suffix_copy_len_matches_remaining_tail",
      "fine_trace_step": 8,
      "description": "`fio_keyword_replace()` saves the original buffer pointer in `o_org`, advances `opt` past the matched keyword, and then computes the suffix copy length from the pointer delta `opt - o_org - 1` instead of the remaining suffix length. On the exact witness, this requests 5 bytes from a suffix whose actual remaining length is only 1; the patch corrects the third argument to `strlen(opt)`."
    },
    {
      "invariant_id": "n_sink_suffix_copy_reads_past_remaining_tail",
      "role": "sink",
      "file": "options.c",
      "function": "fio_keyword_replace",
      "line": 5121,
      "operands": [
        "strlen(opt)",
        "opt - o_org - 1"
      ],
      "relation": {
        "op": "lt",
        "left": "strlen(opt)",
        "right": "opt - o_org - 1"
      },
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_sink_suffix_copy_reads_past_remaining_tail",
      "fine_trace_step": 9,
      "description": "AddressSanitizer crash site. The same `memcpy` uses the miscomputed 5-byte length to read from `opt`, which points at the 2-byte tail `\\xff\\0`, so the source read crosses the right edge of the 8-byte heap buffer returned by `fio_option_dup_subs()`."
    }
  ],
